  "full_response": "A **load balancer** plays a crucial role in web application architecture by distributing incoming network traffic across multiple servers to ensure **high availability, scalability, reliability, and performance**. Here’s a breakdown of its key roles:\n\n### **1. Traffic Distribution (Load Balancing)**\n   - Distributes client requests (HTTP/HTTPS, TCP, UDP) across multiple backend servers (e.g., web servers, application servers, databases) to prevent any single server from becoming overwhelmed.\n   - Uses algorithms like:\n     - **Round Robin** (sequential distribution)\n     - **Least Connections** (sends traffic to the least busy server)\n     - **IP Hash** (consistent routing based on client IP)\n     - **Weighted Round Robin** (prioritizes higher-capacity servers)\n\n### **2. High Availability & Fault Tolerance**\n   - Monitors server health (via **health checks**) and automatically removes unhealthy servers from the pool, redirecting traffic to healthy ones.\n   - Prevents downtime by ensuring that if one server fails, others handle the load seamlessly.\n\n### **3. Scalability**\n   - Enables **horizontal scaling** by adding more servers to handle increased traffic without downtime.\n   - Works with **auto-scaling groups** (e.g., AWS Auto Scaling, Kubernetes) to dynamically adjust resources.\n\n### **4. SSL/TLS Termination**\n   - Offloads **SSL/TLS encryption/decryption** from backend servers, reducing their computational load.\n   - Centralizes certificate management (e.g., Let’s Encrypt, AWS ACM).\n\n### **5. Session Persistence (Sticky Sessions)**\n   - Ensures a user’s requests are consistently routed to the same backend server (useful for stateful applications like shopping carts).\n   - Implemented via **cookies** or **IP-based persistence**.\n\n### **6. Security & DDoS Protection**\n   - Acts as a **reverse proxy**, hiding backend servers from direct exposure to the internet.\n   - Can integrate with **Web Application Firewalls (WAFs)** to filter malicious traffic (e.g., SQL injection, XSS).\n   - Mitigates **DDoS attacks** by distributing traffic and rate-limiting requests.\n\n### **7. Caching & Compression**\n   - Some load balancers (e.g., **NGINX, HAProxy, AWS ALB**) support:\n     - **Static content caching** (reducing backend load).\n",
